{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"f9c5f11b970443c13bff144cdb7a40c1d11592f49c0794f0148a1b61355c7a5a","occurred_at":"2026-11-23T05:46:19Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[1717,1721]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/test_vm_feasibility.py","quoted_text":"        reboot = {\"before\": self._snapshot(10, \"i1\", \"boot-1\"),\n                  \"after\": self._snapshot(11, \"i2\", \"boot-1\"),\n                  \"after_phase\": self._refusals(),\n                  \"qemu_pid_before\": 99, \"qemu_pid_after\": 99,\n                  \"qemu_identity_verified\": True}","reason":"The same-boot test fixture omits the top-level `boot_id_before` and `boot_id_after` fields even though the test asserts `boot_id_changed` is false. That assertion can be satisfied because both values are missing rather than because the observed boot IDs are explicitly equal, so the test does not exercise the intended same-boot boundary. Sibling reboot fixtures set these fields, and the minimal fix is to set both to `\"boot-1\"` here.","target":"199a4d9d782b18a4e267cd7298517741ef168249"},"finding_id":"48ced790d930e5118a0328af23725fb8c8c520176903b7a5d6ee876f5c5149d2","previous_event_id":null,"review_id":"6e872d4037c11824c77d6a11cb37ab2501d08d2570bbae5bd7192d5ebd0c191c"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:48ced790d930e5118a0328af23725fb8c8c520176903b7a5d6ee876f5c5149d2:f2808bf0fec3df48261f268ce3493206f7ac59d97278fc607984c2562266e8f4"}